Article 2: Foreign investment within the territory of the People's Republic of China (hereinafter referred to as within China) shall be governed by this Law.
For the purposes of this Law, "foreign investment" refers to investment activities carried out directly or indirectly within China by foreign natural persons, enterprises or other organizations (hereinafter referred to as foreign investors), including the following circumstances:
(1) Foreign investors establish foreign-invested enterprises within China alone or together with other investors;
(2) Foreign investors acquire shares, equities, property shares or other similar rights and interests in enterprises within China;
(3) Foreign investors invest in new construction projects within China alone or together with other investors;
(4) Other forms of investment specified by laws, administrative regulations or the State Council.
For the purposes of this Law, "foreign-invested enterprise" refers to an enterprise established within China by registration in accordance with Chinese law, wholly or partly invested by foreign investors.
